1
00:00:02,260 --> 00:00:04,630
This is an official Two Point Museum demonstration.

2
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:08,330
A circular ride is positioned, then its entrance is inspected up close.

3
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:11,150
One image contains several different decisions.

4
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:14,230
Another excerpt moves a new ride placement preview.

5
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:17,147
Choosing the attraction and its location is a broader

6
00:00:17,163 --> 00:00:20,050
question than choosing the color of a small decoration.

7
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:24,547
This footage comes from a public demonstration
and additional-content preview in 2026.

8
00:00:24,563 --> 00:00:27,937
We will organize our own design notes from the visible actions.

9
00:00:27,953 --> 00:00:31,647
If a ride, an entrance, and one adjustment value are all

10
00:00:31,663 --> 00:00:34,950
listed at the same level, where should a reader start?

11
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:38,480
We will build that reading order with a hierarchical outline.

12
00:00:40,721 --> 00:00:43,747
An outline does more than indent a long list.

13
00:00:43,897 --> 00:00:49,307
A parent first defines a question, and its children
expand the information needed to answer it.

14
00:00:49,557 --> 00:00:55,947
For example, put placement, track design, and entrance
connection under the goal of visitors using a ride.

15
00:00:56,117 --> 00:00:58,927
This is our explanatory structure based on the footage.

16
00:00:59,137 --> 00:01:02,127
A height adjustment belongs beneath track design.

17
00:01:02,317 --> 00:01:07,944
Separating goals, features, and values lets the reader
understand the whole before individual details.

18
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:11,847
First write one sentence describing what this branch explains.

19
00:01:12,077 --> 00:01:16,937
When an item does not answer that question,
reconsider the parent label or the item’s location.

20
00:01:17,667 --> 00:01:19,797
Now watch the track being adjusted.

21
00:01:19,987 --> 00:01:21,937
An endpoint preview appears first.

22
00:01:22,027 --> 00:01:26,877
In a separate shot, the curve grows toward a neighboring attraction.

23
00:01:27,147 --> 00:01:29,677
Only part of the track changes on screen.

24
00:01:29,867 --> 00:01:33,314
We can separate deciding where the whole attraction belongs

25
00:01:33,330 --> 00:01:36,517
from deciding how this particular section should bend.

26
00:01:36,587 --> 00:01:40,337
As the camera approaches, the selected
endpoint and adjustment points become visible.

27
00:01:40,547 --> 00:01:43,194
Notes about this action could place connection

28
00:01:43,210 --> 00:01:45,937
position and curve adjustment under track design.

29
00:01:46,254 --> 00:01:50,237
Another adjustment changes the curve’s shape and support position.

30
00:01:50,547 --> 00:01:52,814
A feature name alone would leave out

31
00:01:52,830 --> 00:01:54,557
what the player can actually change.

32
00:01:54,727 --> 00:01:58,437
Listing every value at the top would bury the overall plan.

33
00:01:58,787 --> 00:02:01,594
That is why rules for this visible section

34
00:02:01,610 --> 00:02:03,537
belong below the feature that uses it.

35
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:09,683
Children of one parent should answer questions of a comparable scale.

36
00:02:09,833 --> 00:02:14,383
Putting a single height value beside attraction
placement mixes a feature with a detail.

37
00:02:14,573 --> 00:02:19,743
Put placement, track design, and entrance connection beside
one another, with height and rotation under track design.

38
00:02:19,973 --> 00:02:23,323
Indentation communicates containment, not decoration.

39
00:02:23,753 --> 00:02:26,363
There is no requirement to use exactly three levels.

40
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:29,243
An undecided value can remain a question.

41
00:02:29,633 --> 00:02:33,420
What matters is being able to find the feature that owns each detail.

42
00:02:33,436 --> 00:02:38,983
Read the sibling items and check whether they ask similarly sized questions.

43
00:02:39,293 --> 00:02:43,013
If one does not, move it deeper or add a parent that properly contains it.

44
00:02:43,733 --> 00:02:47,303
From another angle, the station and track appear together.

45
00:02:47,553 --> 00:02:49,840
Reading the whole requires more context

46
00:02:49,856 --> 00:02:52,303
than the single value currently selected.

47
00:02:52,533 --> 00:02:56,543
Watch another shot of successive track-curve adjustments.

48
00:02:56,913 --> 00:02:59,000
As the camera and selection point change, the question

49
00:02:59,016 --> 00:03:01,823
being checked at the detail level changes too.

50
00:03:01,913 --> 00:03:05,200
If every detailed rule stays expanded, it becomes harder to

51
00:03:05,216 --> 00:03:08,323
scan the main branches for the station and track design.

52
00:03:08,573 --> 00:03:10,470
Choose the branch needed for the current review.

53
00:03:10,486 --> 00:03:14,223
In the next excerpt, a large loop changes shape.

54
00:03:14,713 --> 00:03:17,440
When reviewing height and tilt, we

55
00:03:17,456 --> 00:03:19,523
can expand the notes about that part.

56
00:03:19,757 --> 00:03:22,320
The detailed rules do not disappear

57
00:03:22,336 --> 00:03:23,963
when the camera moves farther away.

58
00:03:24,333 --> 00:03:27,400
As with this change of viewpoint, we read the whole document,

59
00:03:27,416 --> 00:03:30,523
move down to its details, and return to the broader heading.

60
00:03:30,973 --> 00:03:33,500
Camera controls and document

61
00:03:33,516 --> 00:03:35,463
folding are not the same system.

62
00:03:35,713 --> 00:03:37,840
We are borrowing the change in observation

63
00:03:37,856 --> 00:03:39,803
scale to design a useful reading order.

64
00:03:41,667 --> 00:03:44,797
Folding temporarily hides child items.

65
00:03:44,927 --> 00:03:50,177
It preserves the details while leaving parent headings
visible for reading the broad structure of a design.

66
00:03:50,347 --> 00:03:55,757
Collapse feature details for an overview, then
expand the track branch when reviewing its rules.

67
00:03:55,907 --> 00:03:58,957
Different readers do not need to see the same level of detail.

68
00:03:59,087 --> 00:04:02,957
A collapsed heading must still communicate its scope.

69
00:04:03,127 --> 00:04:07,374
A vague label such as “miscellaneous” hides what
belongs inside as soon as the branch is folded.

70
00:04:07,390 --> 00:04:12,597
Scan the collapsed outline and predict where a needed rule belongs.

71
00:04:12,647 --> 00:04:16,787
Finding it where expected shows that the
headings and structure are helping the reader.

72
00:04:17,517 --> 00:04:20,427
A support near the loop is selected.

73
00:04:20,697 --> 00:04:23,324
As the selected track changes, neighboring

74
00:04:23,340 --> 00:04:26,087
rails and the station remain visible together.

75
00:04:26,297 --> 00:04:28,984
Another excerpt changes a red preview’s

76
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,207
tilt and footprint near the ground.

77
00:04:31,397 --> 00:04:33,864
Notes about this section can keep the adjustable

78
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:35,927
object and its check conditions together.

79
00:04:36,177 --> 00:04:40,347
The visible sections are not an unrelated list of words.

80
00:04:40,517 --> 00:04:42,284
Knowing which track endpoint is being edited

81
00:04:42,300 --> 00:04:44,564
provides context for the support description.

82
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:48,047
The next excerpt moves around a neighboring loop.

83
00:04:48,577 --> 00:04:50,444
It checks how the larger arrangement connects

84
00:04:50,460 --> 00:04:52,527
before returning to the selected part.

85
00:04:52,957 --> 00:04:56,764
If we move this section beneath another feature in our document, its notes

86
00:04:56,780 --> 00:05:00,787
about height and connection conditions should normally move with it.

87
00:05:00,917 --> 00:05:05,007
The last excerpt again changes a nearby curve through a support adjustment.

88
00:05:05,417 --> 00:05:07,964
Moving only the heading and leaving its rules

89
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:10,847
behind can remove the context those rules need.

90
00:05:11,137 --> 00:05:14,107
This comparison concerns moving branches in a document.

91
00:05:14,457 --> 00:05:17,164
It does not claim that every related game rule

92
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:19,547
automatically follows a moved track section.

93
00:05:21,417 --> 00:05:26,907
Treat a heading and its children as one branch when moving an outline.

94
00:05:27,117 --> 00:05:30,727
Moving only the heading can leave the detailed rules in their old location.

95
00:05:30,897 --> 00:05:33,807
Fold the branch, move it, and expand it again.

96
00:05:33,897 --> 00:05:40,567
Checking that the item count is unchanged differs from
checking whether the contents still fit their new parent.

97
00:05:40,637 --> 00:05:47,047
A height rule placed under entrance connection
keeps its words but gains an awkward relationship.

98
00:05:47,077 --> 00:05:50,834
Read the new parent again to see whether it asks the question that rule answers.

99
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:54,487
Reordering is a chance to reconsider the design.

100
00:05:54,717 --> 00:06:00,617
Finishing a move does not prove the structure is
correct; review the meaning of the grouped contents.

101
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:04,980
In another track-editing excerpt, a new curve preview changes

102
00:06:04,996 --> 00:06:08,240
beside existing rails. Describing one section still

103
00:06:08,256 --> 00:06:11,423
requires considering its relationship to its surroundings.

104
00:06:11,853 --> 00:06:16,163
Notes about the selected section’s length or shape can live beneath it.

105
00:06:16,413 --> 00:06:19,440
Conditions to check where it meets another track

106
00:06:19,456 --> 00:06:22,043
can be cross-references between the two branches.

107
00:06:22,253 --> 00:06:26,283
A red track and support then move beside neighboring loops.

108
00:06:26,453 --> 00:06:28,900
The preview and its color do not show that

109
00:06:28,916 --> 00:06:30,650
every connection condition has been resolved.

110
00:06:30,666 --> 00:06:33,623
A later excerpt also shows collision entries.

111
00:06:33,873 --> 00:06:36,863
Our notes should retain unresolved checks.

112
00:06:37,153 --> 00:06:41,063
Organizing a clean structure and solving the actual problem are different tasks.

113
00:06:41,293 --> 00:06:43,823
Now inspect the entrance of a separate attraction up close.

114
00:06:43,933 --> 00:06:47,040
Entrance notes are different from track adjustment

115
00:06:47,056 --> 00:06:49,903
values, but both relate to the goal of using a ride.

116
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:52,623
Watch another excerpt repositioning a golden flower decoration.

117
00:06:52,753 --> 00:06:55,740
Its location is visible, but this shot does not

118
00:06:55,756 --> 00:06:59,400
establish an improvement in visitor satisfaction.

119
00:06:59,416 --> 00:07:01,660
Keep questions about possible relationships

120
00:07:01,676 --> 00:07:04,223
between decoration and access as separate links.

121
00:07:04,413 --> 00:07:07,200
Pointing to one authoritative item is easier to

122
00:07:07,216 --> 00:07:09,893
maintain than copying the same rule into two branches.

123
00:07:11,617 --> 00:07:15,767
Being under a parent means belonging in its explanation.

124
00:07:15,997 --> 00:07:21,387
It does not necessarily mean it must be built
first or that it causes another feature to work.

125
00:07:21,557 --> 00:07:27,827
If entrance connection and decoration placement refer
to one shared rule, store it once and link to it.

126
00:07:28,037 --> 00:07:30,987
Separate copies can drift when edited independently.

127
00:07:31,077 --> 00:07:37,067
Our proposed structure uses vertical branches
for containment and side arrows for references.

128
00:07:37,337 --> 00:07:40,354
It is not a complete dependency analysis of the game.

129
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:43,487
Do not hide an item merely because it is hard to place.

130
00:07:43,677 --> 00:07:48,307
Reconsider the question it answers and make
relationships needing verification visible as questions.

131
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:53,310
The camera moves along the curved track and looks back toward the station.

132
00:07:53,520 --> 00:07:56,207
Checking only one section’s value can

133
00:07:56,223 --> 00:07:58,490
miss how the entire arrangement connects.

134
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:02,150
Another excerpt returns to the track and selects a different support.

135
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:05,107
A reader of our notes should likewise be able to move from

136
00:08:05,123 --> 00:08:08,350
a broad heading to the particular detail needing review.

137
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:10,127
Adjusting a support changes the loop

138
00:08:10,143 --> 00:08:12,850
while neighboring track remains visible.

139
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:15,007
Check whether the document lets a reader

140
00:08:15,023 --> 00:08:16,937
find which feature this rule serves.

141
00:08:16,953 --> 00:08:20,370
The selected track passes through several shapes in the following excerpt.

142
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:23,090
Our notes should describe what is adjustable and what needs

143
00:08:23,440 --> 00:08:25,850
checking, rather than only judging whether it looks impressive.

144
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:28,427
Some shots show collision entries, and another

145
00:08:28,443 --> 00:08:30,550
moment changes the confirmation indicator.

146
00:08:30,660 --> 00:08:32,787
One changed indicator does not justify

147
00:08:32,803 --> 00:08:34,670
marking every review item complete.

148
00:08:34,832 --> 00:08:38,910
Finally, another support is adjusted and the track is inspected again.

149
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:42,727
We separate these different shots by their visible actions,

150
00:08:42,743 --> 00:08:45,807
rather than joining them into one successful play session.

151
00:08:45,823 --> 00:08:48,947
A design document can be reviewed in the same order: read

152
00:08:48,963 --> 00:08:51,867
the overall goal, find a concrete check condition, then

153
00:08:51,883 --> 00:08:54,420
return upward to see how the condition connects to that goal.

154
00:08:56,150 --> 00:09:00,460
A good outline is not defined by many levels or a tidy appearance.

155
00:09:00,690 --> 00:09:05,600
Readers must be able to find the question they
need and understand which goal its answer serves.

156
00:09:05,870 --> 00:09:08,120
Choose one feature from your design.

157
00:09:08,330 --> 00:09:14,400
Put comparable items beside one another, move detailed rules
below them, and mark references to other branches explicitly.

158
00:09:14,590 --> 00:09:18,180
Fold the outline for an overview, expand the relevant branch, and try moving it.

159
00:09:18,390 --> 00:09:21,540
Keep unanswered questions visible afterward.

160
00:09:21,710 --> 00:09:24,940
An organized document and a verified design remain distinct.

161
00:09:25,073 --> 00:09:31,000
If you want practice turning a design into code, see
the programming coaching link in the description.

162
00:09:31,230 --> 00:09:35,840
The goal is a structure that reveals what
to check next, rather than a longer list.
